# Nothing here runs. Every line is a comment; `crontab -l` shows no patch-watch entry.
# Uncommenting a live line installs live traffic, which requires all of the following:
#   1. Jack's message "GATE A APPROVED". Gate A itself is the two-key check: the
#      LIVE_REQUESTS_ENABLED flag in src/config.py AND PATCHWATCH_GATE_A=APPROVED in the
#      environment. The message is the authorisation; see docs/OPERATIONS.md.
#   2. The notice (docs/project_page.md) published as the README at PROJECT_URL, with the
#      opt-out address jforden@carrollu.edu: DONE 2026-10-23 (JForden/JForden 6e9a5ae).
#   3. The IRB determination: RECEIVED 2026-10-23, not human-subjects research
#      (docs/IRB_DETERMINATION.md). Carroll IT informed.
#   4. docs/analysis_plan.md frozen (title commit "analysis plan v1.0 (frozen)").
#
# Schedule (analysis plan §6, decision D3): daily from S1 through day 14 after the fix
# (2026-10-21), then days 21, 28, 45, 60 and 90; at most 22 snapshots, then remove
# these lines. The dated lines below are exact days, so they cannot drift into a
# 23rd run.
#
# Two runs per day (plan §6, D6), chained on one line: Wisconsin first; the comparison
# states start only when it has finished and exited 0 (`&&`). Separate processes, so a
# halt or complaint in the comparison run cannot cost a Wisconsin reading. A Wisconsin
# kill-switch trip (exit 2) skips that day's comparison run. They never overlap:
# pipeline.RunLock refuses a second concurrent live run (rule 4, one request per IP).
#
# Local time on this machine is Central (America/Chicago); cron uses local time, and
# all timestamps in the database are stored in UTC. Put a line `PW=/path/to/patch-watch`
# at the top of the crontab; the entries below use it.
#
# ── rehearsal (no network at all; safe to enable today) ────────────────────────────
# 0 4 * * 0   cd $PW && .venv/bin/python -X utf8 scripts/run_snapshot.py --mock --label MOCK_WEEKLY >> logs/cron.out 2>&1
#
# ── live daily snapshot, S1 .. day 14 = 2026-11-04 (DO NOT UNCOMMENT BEFORE GATE A) ─
# Set the start day to the actual S1 date when Gate A opens.
# 0 9 24-31 10 *  cd $PW && .venv/bin/python -X utf8 scripts/run_snapshot.py --sample data/wi_frame.csv --region wisconsin --label "WI_$(date +\%Y\%m\%d)" >> logs/cron.out 2>&1 && .venv/bin/python -X utf8 scripts/run_snapshot.py --sample data/wi_frame.csv --region comparison --label "CMP_$(date +\%Y\%m\%d)" >> logs/cron.out 2>&1
